  "live_records": {
    "q-10006": {
      "dom_id": "step-q10006",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & b \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ a & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
