    "q-36179": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36179",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5z=5 \\\\ -x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ x-4y+7z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & a & 5 \\\\ b & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+5z=5 \\\\ -x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ x-4y+7z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=-1,\\,c=5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
